, visit:\nhttps://cdphe.colorado.gov/ozone-pollution-and-your-health\n\nHEALTH INFORMATION...Increasing likelihood of respiratory symptoms\nand breathing discomfort in active children and adults and people\nwith lung disease, such as asthma. Active children and adults, and\npeople with lung disease, such as asthma, should reduce prolonged\nor heavy outdoor exertion during the afternoons and evenings both\nWednesday and Thursday.","ends":"2026-08-27T16:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Weld, CO; Adams, CO; Boulder, CO; Jefferson, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Larimer, CO; Broomfield, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ef315fc5f2168dfb17d9e2dcb4b1708f6edc711f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ef315fc5f2168dfb17d9e2dcb4b1708f6edc711f.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 26 at 4:03PM MDT until August 26 at 7:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Larimer County in north central Colorado...\nincluding the Cameron Peak Burn Scar.\n\n* WHEN...Until 700 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 403 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 1 inch of rain has\nfallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nBuckhorn Creek, North Fork Fish Creek, Cedar Creek, Sheep Creek,\nEld Creek and Miller Fork. Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.50\ninches are expected over the area. This additional rain will\nresult in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Larimer County including the\nCameron Peak Burn Scar.","ends":"2026-08-26T19:00:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Larimer, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.afd532a7932a9eacd07403d58599e8328500439d.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.afd532a7932a9eacd07403d58599e8328500439d.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 26 at 3:55PM MDT until August 26 at 11:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n629 IN EFFECT UNTIL 11 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING\nAREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 13 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nELBERT                LINCOLN\n\nIN NORTH CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nLARIMER\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nADAMS                 ARAPAHOE              BOULDER\nBROOMFIELD            DENVER                DOUGLAS\nJEFFERSON             MORGAN                WASHINGTON\nWELD\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, ARVADA, AURORA, BOULDER,\nBROOMFIELD, CASTLE ROCK, CENTENNIAL, DENVER,\nDENVER INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT, ELIZABETH, FORT COLLINS,\nFORT MORGAN, GREELEY, KIOWA, LAKEWOOD, LIMON, LONGMONT, LOVELAND,\nPARKER, THORNTON, WESTMINSTER, AND WINDSOR.","ends":"2026-08-26T23:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Boulder, CO; Broomfield, CO; Denver, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO; Jefferson, CO; Larimer, CO; Lincoln, CO; Morgan, CO; Washington, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.848b288ba106b48f16a6ef11a13265d46c58da15.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.848b288ba106b48f16a6ef11a13265d46c58da15.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 26 at 3:06PM MDT until August 26 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Debris flows and flooding caused by excessive rainfall is\nexpected.\n\n* WHERE...Central Larimer County in north central Colorado, including\nparts of the Cameron Peak burn area.\n\n* WHEN...Until 600 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nDebris flows causing minor flooding.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 304 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Central Larimer County.","ends":"2026-08-26T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Larimer, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6be35616492a811ce0f7cf1195998ae24ec9cbf0.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.6be35616492a811ce0f7cf1195998ae24ec9cbf0.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-26T17:40:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 261740 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1140 AM MDT Wed Aug 26 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered afternoon/evening thunderstorms expected for theI-25 Corridor and plains. A few storms could become severe, with large hail and strong winds possible. - Thunderstorm coverage decreases Thursday and Friday with mainly isolated high-based showers/","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-08-26T20:23:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Rest of today through Thursday...Scattered thunderstorms will move across the urban corridor and eastern plains late this afternoon and early evening with heavy rain, hail, and strong winds. Warmer and drier air moves in for Thursday with isolated high-based showers/thunderstorms. Gusty outflow winds will accompany the showers/thunderstorms while any rainfall will be light. LONG TERM","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":null,"aviation":{"icao":"KAEJ","distance_km":0,"raw_metar":"METAR KAEJ 262235Z AUTO 31018G23KT 10SM CLR 27/00 A3043 RMK AO2 LTG DSNT S T02650004","temp_f":80,"wind_dir":310,"wind_kt":18,"gust_kt":23,"visibility":"10+","cover":"CLR","flight_category":"VFR","altimeter":1030.6,"observed":1787783700,"raw_taf":null,"url":"ht